### PravahOS — Comprehensive Backend Test Flow
### Based on docs/backend-testing-guide.md
###
### Prerequisites:
###   1. make setup          (Postgres, Qdrant, Neo4j, MinIO, API up)
###   2. ollama serve on host + models pulled:
###        ollama pull minimax-m3:cloud && ollama pull qwen3-embedding:0.6b
###   3. Sample PDF at backend/tests/fixtures/sample.pdf (already committed)
###
### Execution order: run top to bottom. REST Client auto-manages httpOnly cookies
### and `# @name` captures response bodies into {{...}} variables, so the happy
### path chains: upload -> ingest -> generate -> review -> complete -> report.
###
### IMPORTANT: sample.pdf is content-deduped (409 on re-upload). For a repeat run
### against the same DB, delete the old regulation (or use a different PDF) so
### step 5.1 succeeds and {{upload.response.body.$.id}} gets set again.
###
### Load-test the LLM path: /generate runs pypdf + graph + vector + 4-agent
### pipeline, so it is slow (needs Ollama reachable).

# ============================================================
# 1. HEALTH & READINESS
# ============================================================

### 1.1 API health (expect {"status":"ok"})
GET http://localhost:8000/health

# ============================================================
# 2. AUTH — REGISTER
# ============================================================

### 2.1 Register compliance officer (can review MAPs)
# @name register
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@pravah.in",
  "password": "admin123",
  "role": "compliance_officer"
}

### 2.2 Register department manager (RBAC tests)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manager@pravah.in",
  "password": "manager123",
  "role": "department_manager"
}

### 2.3 Register duplicate email (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@pravah.in",
  "password": "admin123",
  "role": "compliance_officer"
}

### 2.4 Register invalid email (expect 422)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "bad123"
}

# ============================================================
# 3. AUTH — LOGIN
# ============================================================

### 3.1 Login as compliance officer (sets cookies)
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@pravah.in",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 3.2 Login wrong password (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@pravah.in",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 3.3 Login nonexistent user (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@pravah.in",
  "password": "nobody123"
}

### 3.4 Login missing password (expect 422)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@pravah.in"
}

# ============================================================
# 4. AUTH — ME / REFRESH / LOGOUT
# ============================================================

### 4.1 Get current user (from cookie)
GET http://localhost:8000/auth/me

### 4.2 Rotate tokens (uses refresh_token cookie)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/refresh

### 4.3 Logout (clears cookies)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/logout

### 4.4 Me after logout (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:8000/auth/me

### 4.5 Re-login for the rest of the flow
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@pravah.in",
  "password": "admin123"
}

# ============================================================
# 5. REGULATIONS — UPLOAD
# ============================================================

### 5.1 Upload sample PDF (valid)
# @name upload
POST http://localhost:8000/regulations/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../fixtures/sample.pdf
------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Smoke Test Circular
------boundary--

### upload another pdf

# @name upload
POST http://localhost:8000/regulations/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="2circular.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../fixtures/2circular.pdf
------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

2nd Smoke Test Circular
------boundary--

### 5.2 Upload same PDF again (expect 409 Conflict — hash dedupe)
POST http://localhost:8000/regulations/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../fixtures/sample.pdf
------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Smoke Test Circular
------boundary--

### 5.3 Upload without auth (expect 401) — requires no cookie jar, run after logout
POST http://localhost:8000/regulations/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

not a real pdf
------boundary--

### 5.4 Upload non-PDF (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/regulations/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="note.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is not a PDF
------boundary--

# ============================================================
# 6. REGULATIONS — LIST / GET / INGEST / GENERATE
# ============================================================

### 6.1 List all regulations
GET http://localhost:8000/regulations/

### 6.2 Get uploaded regulation
GET http://localhost:8000/regulations/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}

### 6.3 Get nonexistent regulation (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:8000/regulations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 6.4 Ingest — pypdf extract + classify (expect clause_count >= 1)
POST http://localhost:8000/regulations/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}/ingest

### 6.5 Generate MAPs — 4-agent LangGraph pipeline (SLOW: Ollama + Qdrant + Neo4j)
# @name generate
POST http://localhost:8000/regulations/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}/generate

# ============================================================
# 7. MAPS — LIST / GET
# ============================================================

### 7.1 List all MAPs
GET http://localhost:8000/maps/

### 7.2 List MAPs filtered by regulation
GET http://localhost:8000/maps/?regulation_id={{upload.response.body.$.id}}

### 7.3 Get first generated MAP
# @name map
GET http://localhost:8000/maps/{{generate.response.body.0.$.id}}

### 7.4 Get nonexistent MAP (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:8000/maps/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ============================================================
# 8. MAPS — REVIEW (compliance_officer/admin only)
# ============================================================

### 8.1 Approve MAP
# @name approved
POST http://localhost:8000/maps/{{generate.response.body.0.$.id}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "approve"
}

### 8.2 Edit MAP (description + deadline)
POST http://localhost:8000/maps/{{generate.response.body.0.$.id}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "edit",
  "description": "Updated: Banks must implement MFA within 60 days",
  "deadline": "2026-12-01T00:00:00Z"
}

### 8.3 Reject MAP
POST http://localhost:8000/maps/{{generate.response.body.0.$.id}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "reject"
}

### 8.4 Invalid review action (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/maps/{{generate.response.body.0.$.id}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "delete"
}

# ============================================================
# 9. MAPS — COMPLETE (evidence upload + validation)
# ============================================================

### 9.1 Complete MAP with evidence (expect completeness_check + coverage)
POST http://localhost:8000/maps/{{generate.response.body.0.$.id}}/complete
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="mfa_evidence.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../fixtures/sample.pdf
------boundary--

### 9.2 Complete with unsupported file type (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/maps/{{generate.response.body.0.$.id}}/complete
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="hack.exe"
Content-Type: application/x-msdownload

malicious content
------boundary--

# ============================================================
# 10. REGULATIONS — GRAPH / SIMULATE
# ============================================================

### 10.1 Dependency graph (expect nodes, edges, critical_path, topological_order)
GET http://localhost:8000/regulations/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}/graph

### 10.2 Digital Twin simulation (expect median/p90/pessimistic + bottleneck)
GET http://localhost:8000/regulations/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}/simulate

# ============================================================
# 11. REPORTS
# ============================================================

### 11.1 Compliance report
GET http://localhost:8000/reports/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}/report

### 11.2 Report for nonexistent regulation (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:8000/reports/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/report

